Description: open Windows programs on VeltOS with a double click
 Double-clicking an .exe or .msi file shows its name, publisher and icon
 and asks whether to install or open it. Installers get their own private
 Windows environment (Wine prefix); programs they create appear in Start.
 Programs that need no installation run in a shared environment and can be
 added to Start. Errors are reported in plain language with a log file.
 .
 Based on Wine; DXVK is enabled on computers with a Vulkan-capable GPU.
 Not every Windows program works; Wine is not a security sandbox.
